      "abstract": "Misinformation is often encountered through speech, where claims are fleeting and verification requires leaving the interaction. We present FactNudger, a wearable system that fact-checks everyday speech and selectively alerts users through a smartwatch. FactNudger transcribes conversation, interprets claims in context, retrieves web evidence, and decides whether to wait for more speech, remain silent, or deliver a haptic nudge. The watch presents a concise rationale, while a companion phone provides supporting sources. FactNudger achieved 77% binary verdict accuracy on 125 sampled AVeriTeC claims and selected the intended action for 40 of 50 conversational edge cases. The demonstration lets attendees experience and inspect real-time fact-checking across false claims, incomplete statements, corrections, repetitions, and context-dependent speech.",
